Phase 2 of the T4 ES-library audit: raise the TypeScript guest's compiler pin
from ES2020 to ES2024, and exclude the lib files the engine does not back.

  PREPARED, NOT APPLIED. Apply from the repository root:
      patch -p1 < guests/typescript/tools/lib-audit/phase2-lib-raise.patch
  then rebuild the fixture (`make typescript-guest`) -- driver.js is compiled to
  QuickJS bytecode and baked into tests/wasm/typescript_guest.wasm, so nothing
  changes until it is rebuilt.

  Generated against guests/typescript/driver.js sha256:9c5456f9539c8be3...
  Evidence: results.json (engine verdicts, real fixture), proposal.json (checker
  verdicts per pin), delta.json (what the raise declares).
  Verified end-to-end: applying this patch to a copy of driver.js and running
  `node dryrun-driver.mjs <copy> --expect proposed` reproduces proposal.json's
  proposed pin exactly, with 0 mismatches.

